def mean_sd(frame,col,scale=1):
    x=pd.to_numeric(frame[col],errors='coerce').dropna()
    if x.empty:return '—'
    return f'{x.mean()*scale:.2f} ± {x.std(ddof=1)*scale:.2f}' if len(x)>1 else f'{x.mean()*scale:.2f}'

extra=['','## 10. Environment implementation research','','The supplied assignment document confirms that the core game lets the agent choose a die value from 1 through 6; a random die is an optional stochastic extension. The original SmartDiceEnv correctly exposes six actions and deterministic transitions. The assignment does not fix overshoot behavior; this implementation stays in place, gives −10, and consumes one move. The goal terminates an episode; the four-times-board-size limit truncates it.','','The Gymnasium registry and third-party environment list and a GitHub search were checked. No matching, verifiably Gymnasium-compatible Snakes and Ladders environment was identified. The surfaced GitHub Snakes and Ladders repository is a jQuery game exercise, not an RL environment. The custom implementation is retained to match the assignment. SB3 DQN, PPO and A2C consume the Gymnasium API directly; both environment checkers run in tests. Search details and access dates are in [environment_research.md](environment_research.md).','','## 11. Reward-cycle investigation','','The original reward can conflict with the intended goal: a ladder start pays +20, ordinary moves cost −1, and the goal pays +100. A positive cycle can outscore termination; the 400-step cap adds no failure penalty. Cumulative reward alone is therefore not a success measure. The saved cycle diagnostics list states, dice actions, rewards, cycle length and cycle reward.','','The separate 100-square reward study used three seeds (211, 223, 227), 5,000 episodes, alpha .10, gamma .90, and the same epsilon schedule for both tabular methods. Each policy was evaluated greedily in a new environment for 100 episodes.','', '| Reward configuration | Q-Learning success | QL moves | QL reward | SARSA success | SARSA moves | SARSA reward |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
